# xfstests that cannot run usefully on spadfs2, passed to ./check -E by
# tests/xfstests_vm.sh. Only tests whose failure would break the tests after
# them belong here; a test that just fails on a missing feature stays in the
# run and is listed in the baseline (tests/HARDWARE-NOTES.md).

# fsstress writes at offsets up to ~670 MB from 20 processes; without
# sparse files every one allocates everything below its offset, the 4 GB
# test device fills, and the test exits before removing its files -- every
# later test then fails with ENOSPC.
generic/013
